# Usage and help message
USAGE = f'''Usage:
Pan_TE [options]

Example:
    # Single genome mode
    Pan_TE --genome genome.fasta --threads 80 --model-dir Your_Path_To_ClassifyTE

    # Pan-genome mode (reference-free PAF)
    Pan_TE --paf all_vs_all.paf --paf-fasta asm1.fna asm2.fna ... --threads 80

    # Enrichment mode (genome + PAF)
    Pan_TE --genome ref.fasta --paf all_vs_all.paf --paf-fasta assemblies.fa --threads 80

    # Pan-genome mode (GFA)
    Pan_TE --gfa pangenome.gfa --threads 80

    # Enrichment mode (genome + GFA)
    Pan_TE --genome ref.fasta --gfa pangenome.gfa --threads 80

Parameters:
[General]
    --genome <string>         Genome file in FASTA format. Required unless --paf or --gfa is provided.
    --model-dir <string>      Provide path to ClassifyTE for classification.

[Other]
    --vcf-dir <string>        Default: NA. Path for VCF, see gfa.list for format.
    --paf <string>           PAF file from all-vs-all genome alignment (FastGA/wfmash/minimap2).
    --paf-fasta <string...>  Assembly FASTA file(s) for PAF. Accepts multiple files.
    --paf-mapping <string>   Optional: chromosome mapping TSV (seqname, assembly_id, chr_id).
    --gfa <string>           GFA file from pangenome graph (minigraph-cactus rGFA or PGGB smoothxg).
    --gfa-ref <string>       Reference path/sample name in GFA (auto-detected if omitted).
    --gfa-mode <string>      Alleles mode (PGGB paths or rGFA+GAF); legacy enables old topology walking.
    --gfa-gaf <string>       Primary GAF for rGFA sample-path recovery.
    --gfa-gaf-fasta <string> Query FASTA used to validate GAF query names and lengths.
    --gfa-window-overlap <int>
                             Overlap for long allele windows, default: 1000 bp.
    --gfa-spacer-length <int>
                             N spacer between packed candidates; default: 0 (separate records).
    --gfa-clean-intermediates
                             Remove candidate FASTA intermediates after manifest generation.
    --anno                   Project all-genome TE/GFF3 annotations onto GFA nodes (requires --gfa and --anno-manifest).
    --anno-only              Run only the new annotation-projection stage; skip TE-library discovery.
    --anno-manifest <tsv>    Per-sample/haplotype annotation manifest; replaces the legacy RepeatMasker anno mode.
    --anno-te-min-fraction <float>
                             Minimum TE-covered fraction for a node/occurrence TE call; default: 0.80.
    --anno-partial-min-fraction <float>
                             Minimum TE-covered fraction for PartialTE; default: 0.10.
    --out-dir <string>       Default: current directory. The work directory.
    --te-looker-bin <string> Path to te-looker dtr binary. Default: TE_LOOKER_BIN or PATH.
    --te-looker-extra-args <string>
                             Extra arguments passed verbatim to "dtr run".
    --te-looker-final-gated Request dtr's verified internal stitch/gate/merge path.
                             Fails before discovery if the binary does not advertise it.
    --te-looker-w <int>      Default: 1 (exact: every k-mer). >1 subsamples k-mers to
                             ~2/(w+1) of their occurrences, cutting te-discover memory
                             roughly proportionally. This CHANGES the seed set, so it is
                             opt-in only; --min-count is re-derived to match.
    --check-env              Verify tools, Perl/Python modules and memory, then exit.
    -M <int>                 Memory limit (in MB), default: 0 (unlimited).
    --threads <int>          Default: 4. Number of threads, preferably in multiples of 4.
    --fragment-size <int>    Default: 40000. Length for fragment.
    --help|-h                Display this help information.

Version: {VERSION}
'''

